# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Course materials — NEVER COMMIT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These folders hold ~94MB of class handouts plus two commercial Kuroshio
# textbooks (Tobira Intermediate Japanese / Tobira Kanji and Vocabulary).
# Committing them would redistribute copyrighted material and bloat the repo.
# They live on disk and are read by the ingest pipeline via MATERIALS_ROOT.
/Foundation 1*/
/Foundation 2/
/Foundation 3/
/Intermediate/
/materials/

# Derived artifacts from ingestion (regenerable, large)
/.work/
*.pdf
*.ppt
*.pptx
*.doc
*.docx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
.dev.vars
.wrangler/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The local copy of the production database
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# scripts/local-db.sh dumps production (read-only) into a container so that
# development never touches the database a hundred students are reading. The
# dump and the fixture exported from it are COURSE MATERIAL — the textbooks and
# the sat papers, page by page — and the textbooks are commercial. They belong
# on a laptop and in a container and nowhere else, least of all in a
# repository.
#
# Named explicitly rather than left to /.work/ above. That rule covers them
# today because that is where they happen to be written; this one says why
# they must never be committed, so moving the work directory cannot quietly
# take the protection with it.
*.dump
*.sql.gz
/.work/prod-*.dump
/.work/quiz-fixture.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python (ingest/)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node (web/)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.open-next/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/

# Playwright artifacts
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Wrangler local preview log
web/.wrangler-preview.log
